## Architectural Memory Rules

These rules are learned from common failure patterns. Apply them in every block:

| Rule | Why |
|------|-----|
| Write the Zod schema before writing the Claude prompt | The prompt must produce a shape the schema can parse. Reverse order causes rework. |
| Test `urgencyGate()` with Mandarin strings before wiring Express route | Chinese character matching has edge cases (full-width punctuation, simplified vs traditional). |
| Chunk RAG content to ~400 tokens at index time | Larger chunks hurt retrieval precision; smaller chunks lose context. |
| Never stream Claude output to the client raw | Stream to server-side buffer → validate with Zod → send structured JSON. |
| TTS endpoint must stream audio, not buffer it | Buffering causes > 1s delay. Use `Response` with `ReadableStream`. |
| Keep prompts in `/lib/prompts.ts` and import them | Inline prompts in route handlers make testing and review impossible. |

